{
  "requirement": "The book preprocessor MUST escape requirement names and link targets when inserting badge HTML. It MUST encode badge label and message text in Shields.io URL path components so punctuation cannot change the badge URL structure.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately cover `requirements.references.safe_badges`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. Requirement names and link targets MUST be HTML-escaped when badge HTML is inserted.\n2. Shields.io label and message text MUST be encoded in URL path components, so punctuation cannot change the URL structure.\n\n**Obligation 2: Shields.io path encoding** (`shield_badge` and `shield_path_component`)\n- `badge_urls_percent_encode_punctuation_and_html_is_escaped` passes the label `a/b?c` and the message `x#y%z&w<v>\"u' café`.\n  - It asserts the exact URL: `a%2Fb%3Fc-x%23y%25z%26w%3Cv%3E%22u%27_caf%C3%A9-006ba8?style=flat-square&amp;labelColor=555`.\n  - That covers `/ ? # % & < > \" '`, a space becoming `_`, multibyte UTF-8, and `&` in the `src` attribute being escaped to `&amp;`.\n  - It also asserts that `alt` is HTML-escaped: `a/b?c x#y%z&amp;w&lt;v&gt;&quot;u&#39; café`.\n- `shields_badge_urls_escape_requirement_names` covers the shields.io-specific `_` → `__` and `-` → `--` doubling, which keeps those characters from altering the label/message separator. It also covers a space in the status badge message (`Determination_false`). It asserts the plain-text `alt`.\n\n**Obligation 1: link targets**\n- `reference_link_targets_are_escaped` gives the target chapter a rendered path containing `&`, `\"`, `<`, `>` and a space. It renders a `{cite}` reference through `reference_badge` and asserts the escaped `href`. It also asserts that the raw `\"q\"` and `<x>` do not appear.\n- `definition_evidence_link_targets_are_escaped` covers the `replace_definitions` badge. It puts a special-character path on the requirements-index chapter. It asserts the escaped evidence `href` and the `title`, and that the raw `a&b`, `\"q\"` and `<x>` are absent from the name link.\n\n**Escaping of requirement names**\n- In `replace_definitions`, the escaped name feeds `title`, `aria-label`, the anchor and the link text.\n- In `reference_badge`, the name reaches the `alt` text through `shield_badge`.\n- The `alt` escaping is tested with HTML-special characters in `badge_urls_percent_encode_punctuation_and_html_is_escaped`.\n- The `escape_html(&full_name)` call in `replace_definitions` is guarded by `valid_name`. A comment there says valid names contain no HTML-special characters, so it cannot be driven with a special-character name through the preprocessor. It uses the same `escape_html` function the tests exercise elsewhere. I see no gap in leaving it untested.\n\n**Other badge sites**\nThe index and detail pages build their links as Markdown, and the badge in `render_detail_sections` goes through `shield_badge`. No separate unescaped HTML badge path turned up in my search.\n\nAll four tests carry `{test}` references to the requirement. I found no unmarked relevant tests and no missing scenario.",
  "references": "f360114568ba3231c5da9e9b2c91d05137e8af13c41c17d23dea91167c755e21",
